    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for 2026-06-11 is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns today\u2019s highest efficiency score of 75.30. Despite facing a competent arm in Woo (3.42 xERA), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole, providing the highest ceiling for R and HR production. **Kyle Tucker** (68.96) and **Andy Pages** (63.73) follow as strong plays against Keller, M (4.37 xERA). While **Kyle Tucker** is batting lower in the order than preferred, his base projection remains elite, and **Andy Pages** leverages an 8% boost from his position at the top of the lineup to maintain his status as a recommended start.\n\nDecision-making on the fringe remains focused on maximizing efficiency within our daily caps. **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Josh Jung** (57.72) both occupy the \"Marginal\" threshold but are preferred starts due to their favorable matchups against Kelly, M and Wacha, respectively. **Liam Hicks** benefits from a distinct platoon edge and leadoff duties, which narrowly keeps him ahead of the bench options. **Coby Mayo** (41.80) is the most volatile start today; while he carries a positive park factor, the combination of his low batting order and the skill of Woo makes him a high-risk play. We are monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** closely, as their absence due to injury continues to force us into sub-optimal utilization of our depth. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** unavailable today, the Waves are forced to lean on the current lineup to maintain pace in the scarcity-driven SB category, where we are missing the high-end speed upside usually provided by players like **Nasim Nunez** or **Brayan Rocchio**.",
